{
  "about": [
    "What a parameter is doing, as a corpus: what is driving it, a moment, and the",
    "value that comes out. Read by two test suites \u2014 a native Rust one in",
    "crates/pult-render-wasm/tests, and a vitest one in frontend/src/lib that loads",
    "the same crate compiled to wasm and asks it the same questions.",
    "",
    "This file is what replaced writing the evaluator twice. `values-as-functions`",
    "declined to translate the arithmetic into TypeScript \u2014 the surface is easings,",
    "curves, step lists, spread, phase, direction, width, master rates, priority and",
    "home fallback, and two of it would drift \u2014 so what has to be guarded is not two",
    "implementations agreeing but two *compilations* of one agreeing. A wasm build",
    "that optimises a float differently, or a boundary that packs a colour wrong, is",
    "exactly the failure this catches, and it shows up here rather than as a screen",
    "disagreeing with the lamps.",
    "",
    "Every case names one parameter, so a failure reads as a sentence."
  ],
